  "footnote": "All major courses require a letter grade of B- or better. No course may satisfy two major requirements. Admission to the major requires one completed RELST content course. Select courses with the major advisor. One advanced language course directly related to the academic study of religion may count by petition only; language study is encouraged, not required. Non-RELST cross-listings and the petitioned language course need advisor confirmation and a manual checklist adjustment. Honors is optional: RELST 4995 then RELST 4996 over two consecutive semesters, up to 8 credits, may satisfy the two advanced-course requirements. Honors eligibility requires a 3.3 cumulative average, a 3.5 major average and no major grade below B-; apply by mid-March of junior year and complete the thesis and defense.",
